Deterministic target-tracking audit - conclusion
=================================================

Data: data/measurements.npz - 95 uniform time steps (dt = 1.0), two channels:
channel 0 = range (strictly positive, U-shaped, minimum 0.523 at t=36),
channel 1 = bearing in (-pi, pi] with exactly one +/-pi wrap (t=5->6).
Masked (missing) blocks: range t=22..31, bearing t=55..63. These blocks are
SKIPPED in the likelihood; no replacement observations are generated.

Method: bootstrap particle filter, N=1200 (cap 1500), fixed seed 42, log-domain
weights, systematic resampling when ESS < N/2. State = [x, y, vx, vy, beta_b,
beta_r]; beta_* are slowly drifting additive sensor-bias random walks. Motion is
constant velocity with switching process noise (nominal/maneuver Markov chain per
particle plus a 2% i.i.d. strong-kick fraction) so maneuvering intervals are
absorbed by weight competition instead of a fixed clean model. Likelihood is
per-channel: Gaussian mixture (0.9 main / 0.1 wide tail) for range and for the
WRAPPED bearing innovation, which makes the five correlated two-channel outlier
steps (t ~ 17, 41, 49, 72, 79) non-destructive without measurement editing.
Mild adaptive sigma inflation (max 4x) is applied if ESS drops below 15% of N;
the resampling threshold was NOT lowered.

IMPORTANT - diagnostic semantics: the true state trajectory is not public, so the
rmse_pos / rmse_vel / nees columns are FILTER-INTERNAL PROXIES, not true errors:
  rmse_pos = RMS position-equivalent measurement residual (range residual and
             bearing residual times predicted range);
  rmse_vel = dynamics-consistency proxy || v_est(t) - (p_est(t)-p_est(t-1))/dt ||;
  nees     = normalized innovation squared (NIS) of the available channels
             against the predicted measurement covariance.
bearing_residual_mean/std use a documented finite fallback of 0.0 at t=55..63,
where the bearing channel is masked.

Key findings:
  - Angle wrap events detected on the OBSERVATIONS (|d bearing| > pi criterion):
    1 (at t=5->6); angle_wrapping_detected = True.
  - Resampling performed 54 times; ESS min = 5.8,
    ESS mean = 566.5; weight degeneracy detected =
    True.
  - Mean position-fit proxy 0.0541, mean velocity-consistency
    proxy 0.0416, mean/median NIS proxy 1.648/0.032.
  - Final bias-state estimates: bearing bias +0.0393 rad, range bias
    +0.3310 (slow drift tracked, bounded).
  - The record is not one global constant-velocity motion: per-segment CV fits
    fit at noise level for t=0..21 and t=64..94 but are rejected for t=32..54,
    where the implied trajectory swings around the sensor (bearing rate peaks
    near 0.45 rad/step) and the unwrapped bearing rate reverses sign afterwards.
    The filter's switching process noise covers this maneuvering interval.

Uncertainties: bearing reference axis/sign and the sensor origin are assumed
(+x axis, CCW, origin), not inferable from the file alone; the split between
target maneuvering and slow bias drift is only partially identifiable with a
single sensor, and both effects are modeled rather than resolved.
